{
  "_comment": [
    "Copy to <data_dir>/config/sweep.json and edit. Read by deploy/run-conductor-scheduled.ps1.",
    "This file holds the EXCEPTIONS; discovery is the default. Every live thread of a project in",
    "clones is found each tick, whether or not it is listed below.",
    "",
    "clones (project -> the implementer's own absolute CLONE path) is the one place a discovered",
    "thread's repo_dir comes from — it is never guessed from other candidates. Declare every",
    "project you want discovery to work for, including ones that already have candidates (a",
    "candidate's repo_dir applies only to that one thread). A shape error (not an object, a blank",
    "key or value) stops the tick. A per-project environment problem (relative path, missing",
    "directory, the daemon's own checkout, a linked worktree) does not: only that project's",
    "threads are refused, with the reason, in the digest. A project with no clones entry is still",
    "scanned and shown as 'clones 未登録'.",
    "",
    "intake is OPTIONAL: { mode: 'shadow' | 'on', max_idle_days: <positive number> }, default",
    "shadow / 14. A live thread NOT listed below joins the tick's candidates only when ALL hold:",
    "mode is 'on', its project's clone is usable, its last activity (the listing's",
    "last_activity_at) is at most max_idle_days old, and it is not in exclude. Otherwise it",
    "appears in the digest's 未登録（登録不可） section as 登録予定（shadow）, 放置, 時刻不明",
    "(last_activity_at missing or unparseable) or 登録不可 with the reason, or only as a count for",
    "除外 — never silently ignored, and never in any state file. If a project's listing has items",
    "with no last_activity_at key at all, the tick log WARNs and the 時刻不明 header shows the",
    "count (N/M). Switch to 'on' only after a human has read the shadow",
    "list; it is not the switch for keeping already-running threads alive (list those below).",
    "",
    "exclude is OPTIONAL: [\"<project>/<thread_id>\", ...] — discovered threads never to pick up.",
    "",
    "candidates: order is priority for the threads listed here — the sweep walks this list",
    "head-first and stops at the first candidate that actually ran rounds; discovered threads come",
    "after them (by clones order, then oldest update first). A listed thread is always a",
    "candidate: mode, exclude, max_idle_days and the time checks never apply to it. A candidate's",
    "repo_dir that differs from clones[project] gets a WARN in the tick log and is used as given.",
    "",
    "Each candidate needs all three fields. repo_dir is the implementer's own CLONE for that",
    "project (not a linked worktree, and never the checkout the daemon itself is running from —",
    "the implementer would be editing its own running code).",
    "",
    "auto_gate is OPTIONAL: { mode: 'dry-run' | 'on', auto_gate_daily_cap: 30, gate_bases:",
    "['main', 'develop'] } (T-gate-fires-on-pr-open). The tick fires the first PR-gate of an",
    "open PR by posting NEXT: pr-review into the thread its body names. Absent or dry-run:",
    "every PR is judged and logged, nothing is posted. Compare that log before switching on.",
    "It scans every clones project, whether or not a candidate names it; a held project is skipped.",
    "",
    "owner_map is OPTIONAL. When present it turns on the resource-axis HOLD gate — a HOLD on the",
    "listed 'owning project' also stops every candidate that writes to the matching repo, even",
    "when those candidates belong to a different chatroom project. See the specifying thread",
    "'T-loop-control-keyed-by-project-resource-is-the-repo' §5a v2 for the design. The KEY is a",
    "predicted resource identity in the shape <host>/<org>/<repo>, lowercased; the sweep's tick",
    "log prints the resource it observed for each repo_dir so you can copy the exact string in",
    "without re-typing. Missing owner_map = gate OFF (fully backward compatible; behaviour is",
    "then identical to before the resource axis existed).",
    "",
    "projects is OPTIONAL: chatroom projects whose open threads the park-wake tick reads and",
    "classifies (the digest's 停止理由 line) even when no candidate below names them, so a thread",
    "outside the sweep is not left unseen. The scan is the union of these and the candidates'",
    "projects; nothing is launched for a project listed only here. The scan for live threads NOT",
    "listed below (discovery above) covers this union plus the clones keys. Missing projects = the",
    "candidates' projects only (behaviour before the key existed). A malformed value is named in",
    "the digest as 'sweep.json:projects' and scans nothing extra; it does not stop the sweep.",
    "",
    "Do NOT list T-pr-review-* threads: they resolve to `NEXT: pr-review <ref>`, which fires the",
    "Tier B PR-gate against the paid Lexora/Gemini backend. Driving those from an unattended sweep",
    "would spend money on a timer, so it stays an explicit human action."
  ],
  "projects": [
    "spirrow-magickit"
  ],
  "clones": {
    "spirrow-mindwire": "C:/workspace/sandbox/mindwire-impl",
    "spirrow-voxelworld": "C:/workspace/sandbox/voxelworld-impl"
  },
  "intake": {
    "mode": "shadow",
    "max_idle_days": 14
  },
  "exclude": [
    "spirrow-mindwire/T-example-thread-not-to-discover"
  ],
  "owner_map": {
    "github.com/spirrowgames/spirrow-mindwire": "spirrow-mindwire",
    "github.com/spirrowgames/spirrow-voxelworld": "spirrow-voxelworld"
  },
  "candidates": [
    {
      "project": "spirrow-voxelworld",
      "thread_id": "T-example-live-design-thread",
      "repo_dir": "C:/workspace/sandbox/voxelworld-impl"
    },
    {
      "project": "spirrow-mindwire",
      "thread_id": "T-example-mindwire-thread",
      "repo_dir": "C:/workspace/sandbox/mindwire-impl"
    }
  ]
}
